/P 85 0 R
/E (WHY IS KPUD ASKING VOTERS FOR AUTHORITY TO ACQUIRE OR CONSTRUCT ELECTRIC FACILITIES BEFORE CONDUCTING A FEASIBILITY STUDY?)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Community members have asked KPUD to consider whether it could help address electric service costs and other concerns. A comprehensive feasibility study is estimated to cost between $300,000 and $500,000. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Voters in other Washington communities have considered similar measures. Of four electric authority measures presented to voters in 2008 and 2012, one was approved and three were not. Given the significant cost of a comprehensive feasibility study and voting history for similar measures, the Board determined that it was prudent to seek voter direction first.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (WHAT HAPPENS AFTER THE FEASIBILITY STUDY? )
/Pg 12 0 R
