/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (No, Proposition 1 would not immediately change property taxes or electric rates.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (KPUD currently levies a property tax of approximately $0.045 per $1,000 of assessed property value, or about $22.50 per year on a $500,000 home. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Under state law, regular property-tax revenue generally may increase by no more than 1% each year, plus amounts resulting from new construction and other permitted adjustments. An increase beyond the regular levy limit, known as a levy lid lift, requires voter approval. Proposition 1 does not authorize a property-tax increase or constitute a levy lid lift.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
